A||||7||Shiner||Anybody in the restaurant biz?||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||11-29-2000||11:27 PM||||This kind of goes along with the topic about jobs.  Does anybody else here work in a restaurant?  Currently, I am the cook/dishwasher/prep-monkey/bus boy/occasional waitor/occasional pizza maker at a small italian restaurant down the street from me.  Does it drive everybody else to drinking, or is it just me?  Five things I hate about restaurants are:<P>1) The parents who come in with mini-me's and let the kid roam the place like a wild animal. Spilling choclate milk, pizza, spaghetti, and vomit all in once place is barely human, let alone proper behaviour for a 3 year old child.<P>2) There always has to be some mullet-wearing redneck that comes it ten minutes before closing to have a few beers.  We end up leaving way late because we don't kick him out.  Mullet guys are scary.<P>3) I could go into work smelling of daisies and sugar pies, but I always come out smelling like cheese steaks and burned ass.<P>4) The people who are loaded with dough, but come in and order crap like 2 meat balls and a salad.  Then they haggle over the ten dollar bill they racked up over the three hours they sat there and leached.  Then they pull out a roll of twenty dollar bills out of their pocket.  &lt;^&gt;<P>5) The two Morocan guys you work with steal your cigarettes all the time, because aparently that is normal behaviour over there.  <P>I am sure there is more to come, wait for the update  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cheever2||11-29-2000||11:59 PM||||Okay, I've been on another planet, but what's a mullet?  Is that anything like a tuke (sp)?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||11-30-2000||12:03 AM||||Boy, that brings back memories.  When I was 16 (28 years ago!), I worked in a pizza place.  Experienced most of what you have (except I never smoked). <P>You'll appreciate this.  Someone ordered a pizza with "the works" at about 5 P.M.  It's to go, so when it's done I "bag it up" and put it on top of the oven.  The knucklehead never picked it up.  Figured it was some jerk playing a prank.  Finally at about 10:30 P.M.  I throw it in the garbage.  About 11:55 P.M. the guy comes in wanting the pizza!!  We close at midnight!  If I make him a new pizza now, it would be 12:30 before it's done, and then by the time we cleaned up and closed it's 1 a.m.  So I figure if the guy is that lame, no way I'm making a new one.  So I drag the garbage can out of view, pull the pizza out of all the crud, (hey, it's wrapped in foil and a bag), put it in a new bag, and take it out to him.  Then he says, "Oh, I'll eat it here!"  Man, I figured if the pizza was bad I'd be long gone before he figured it out.  So I unwrapped it and put it back together the best I could and served it to him.  I was sweating it, but he never complained.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||12-01-2000||02:35 AM||||Cheve,<BR> A mullet is a hair style, which may also be known as "hockey hair".  It's when the person has longer hair in the back, and a normal short haircut in the front.  Until you know how to recognise and catagorise mullets, you won't know how many there really are.  These are people you see in the street, maybe even your co-workers.  YOU could even have a mullet and not know it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Lobe,<BR> Right on!!!  I got a kick out of that story!<P>And listen to this!!  Somebody was about 30 minutes late to pick up a pizza today.  I was starting to wonder if they were coming, when the phone rang.  It was her, calling to say she couldn't pick up the pizza because a train derailed on the bridge, and she couldn't get over here to PA.  Of course I was polite, and told her no problem and thanks for calling.  She must have forgotten: the store is 30 yards away from the bridge.  Everything was normal when I went outside.  <P> Some people....||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-01-2000||09:27 PM||||Hmmm.... My favorite is puzzle pizza. You know the ones that want diferant stuff on practically every slice. There was one guy in the shop I worked in NY that pulled one of these and got pissed when I didn't understand his order. He left pieless and pissed. To this day I still have no clue what the hell he was trying to describe....||||reg||1
Z||000005||frontal lobe||12-02-2000||02:07 AM||||LOL!  Train derailment.  Yeah, I can't TELL you how often that makes me late for somewhere.<P>Hey Shiner, when I worked in the pizza place the manager was pretty cool and so we could make our own pizzas while at work and eat all we wanted.  So we would always do that.  But there was one knucklehead that worked there and he was so dense he couldn't even make his own pizzas, so he would always bug ME to make him one--usually at the worst, busiest times.  He was such a pain, so one time I told him "yeah, I'll make you a pizza".  So I put the dough down, put the sauce on, and then before putting the cheese on, I took the lid off a shaker of hot peppers and dumped the whole pile right in the middle of the pizza.  Then I put the cheese and topping over it.  He ate THE WHOLE PIZZA and never said a word.  He didn't have to, though, because I could see the sweat PORING off his forehead.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||12-03-2000||01:44 AM||||Ahh, mullets and hockey hair. Also known as shortlongs, 10-90's and 7-heads. Go to <A HREF="http://www.mulletsgalore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mulletsgalore.com</A>   I guarantee you'll like it!||||reg||1
Z||000007||overlord||12-03-2000||08:53 AM||||ya i kinda work in a resurant..<BR>hotel actually/resterant.<P>but im there all night by myslef usually....so no nasty people to deal with.||||reg||1
